2. Distinguish a slow pathway, an unsupported workable design, and an assembly not yet available. Separate changed routes from increased expenditure and construction costs from continued operation.
3. Explain joint material and Platonic constraints through operating relations, materials, tolerances, and manufacturing. Show how each changes the practical scope of the other.
4. Use Newcomen as the main case of a setting able to support an inefficient first assembly. Develop the causal sequence from prior resources through pumping to changed fuel access and further construction.
